{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraidChargeObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraidChargeObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.borromean_strand_writhes_all_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.borromean_strand_writhes_all_zero","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L186-L198","doc":"**Every strand of the canonical Borromean word carries signed crossing sum\n`0`.**\n\nSo the `±` orientation label that `up-quark.md` and `down-quark.md` use to\nseparate `𝔲` from `𝔡` inside `𝓑₃` is invisible to any per-strand crossing sum:\nthe three components are indistinguishable by that measure.  (The pairwise\nlinking numbers all vanish too — that is the defining property of the Borromean\nrings, and it is why the word is cyclically symmetric of order three.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.strandWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.strandWrithe","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L170-L184","doc":"Signed crossing sum carried by one strand of a braid word on `n` strands.\n\nEach letter `σᵢ^{±1}` is a crossing between the two strands currently at\npositions `i` and `i+1`; it contributes its sign to **both** of them.  The\nrunning list is the one-line notation of the partial permutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.borromean","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L167-L168","doc":"The canonical Borromean baryon `𝓑₃ = (σ₁σ₂⁻¹)³ ∈ B₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.gluonUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.gluonUnit","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L164-L165","doc":"The gluon unit `σ₁σ₂⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.linear_charge_map_refuted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.linear_charge_map_refuted","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L147-L160","doc":"**No linear charge map.**\n\n`Q = c·w` cannot fit the up and down together: their writhes are antisymmetric\n(`+1`, `−1`) while their charges are not (`+2/3`, `−1/3`).  This is the sharpest\nform — it needs no charge-conjugation hypothesis at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.charge_not_factoring_through_writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.charge_not_factoring_through_writhe","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L130-L145","doc":"**A fortiori, not a function of the writhe.**\n\nThis route does not use `antiUp_eq_down`: it needs only that the anti-up and the\ndown carry the *same writhe* `−1`, so any `Q` factoring through the writhe is\nforced to agree on them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.charge_not_factoring_through_braid_element","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.charge_not_factoring_through_braid_element","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L116-L128","doc":"**The Coulomb charge does not factor through the braid element.**\n\nCharge conjugation negates `Q` and acts as the braid mirror.  The mirror of the\nup quark *is* the down quark's braid element (`antiUp_eq_down`), so `Q` would\nhave to give that one word both `−2/3` (as the anti-up) and `−1/3` (as the\ndown). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.quark_writhes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.quark_writhes","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L110-L112","doc":"The quark writhes are `±1`, not `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.writhe_antiUp_eq_writhe_down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.writhe_antiUp_eq_writhe_down","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L105-L108","doc":"The two carry the same writhe, `−1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.antiUp_eq_down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.antiUp_eq_down","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L101-L103","doc":"**Computed, not assumed.**  The braid mirror of the up quark is exactly the\ndown quark's braid element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.downQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.downQuark","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L96-L97","doc":"The down quark's braid element: `σ₁⁻¹`, a negative crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.upQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.upQuark","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L93-L94","doc":"The up quark's braid element: `σ₁`, a positive crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.mirror","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L89-L91","doc":"The braid mirror `σᵢ ↦ σᵢ⁻¹` — charge conjugation, per\n`AntiparticleCrossingReversalContext`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.writhe","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L86-L87","doc":"The writhe: the sum of the crossing signs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.BraidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.QuarkBraid.BraidWord","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/QuarkBraidChargeObstruction.lean#L82-L84","doc":"A braid word: entry `±i` denotes `σᵢ^{±1}`.  Same convention as\n`ChiralFermionBraidWords.lean` and `WritheLevelParity.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}